From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 11:51:24 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 279/297] Meridian: choose the space (Little window, tab menu,
 Peek)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

As in Arc, a page can go to any space:
- Little window: one split button, "Open in <Space>" (the space it is
  in) and a ▾ with every space; picking one opens the page there in the
  main window (with that space's profile). Replaces the separate space
  button and "Open in Meridian".
- A tab's menu (one tab or several): "Open in Space ▸" puts a copy in
  that space and keeps this one, with a toast; "Move to Space ▸" as
  before.
- Peek: "Open as Tab" gets a ▾ (when there are other spaces) to open it
  as a tab in another space, which comes up with it.
The menus take the keyboard: ↓ on the ▾ opens them, arrows move,
Escape goes back to the ▾. New mojom (appended): OpenUrlInSpace,
MoveTabToSpaceAndShow.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
